# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
title    Title
composer Claude
about    The world in its glass cubes, seen from outside before the journey starts: a slow waltz in F like the town's, played on glass. A crystal lead and its echo over a harp, glass harmonica chords, a singing bowl and wind chimes. After a while it turns to D minor and a borrowed Bb minor, then finds its way home to F. Only the main menu plays it, so it only knows explore.
tempo    92
beats    3
steps    4
reverb   0.45

# moods (music/README.md); the main menu only ever plays explore
# mood explore:  lead echo glow chords harp bass bowl tap chimes

voice lead    crystal    vol=1.0  pan=-0.1
voice echo    crystal    vol=0.32 pan=0.45 rev=0.6
voice glow    glassharp  vol=0.32 pan=0.25 rev=0.55
voice chords  glassharp  vol=0.2  pan=-0.3 center=A4 att=0.3 rel=0.6
voice harp    harp       vol=0.45 pan=0.3
voice bass    upright    vol=0.7
voice bowl    bowl       vol=0.28 pan=-0.2 rev=0.6
voice tap     glasstap   vol=0.25 pan=0.35
voice chimes  chimes     vol=0.3  pan=-0.4

# the cubes come into view: two bars of F
pattern intro
chords    | [F]----------- | [Fmaj7]----------- |
harp      | F3- C4- F4- A4- C5- A4- | F3- C4- E4- A4- C5- E5- |
bass      | F2------- C3--- | F2------- C3--- |
bowl      | F4----------- | _ |
chimes    | x... .... .... | .... .... .... |

# F Bb F C | F Dm Gm-C F; the tune opens on the game's motif, 1 2 3 5 4 (F G A C Bb)
